   - note important asymmetries, substitutions, or restrictions
   - highlight cases where one constructional strategy appears to replace another
   - note cases where a function is weakly expressed, constructionally indirect, or absent

Important constraints:

- Work only from the observed F4 data.
- Do NOT assume a predefined inventory of construction types.
- Do NOT force every language into the same constructional schema.
- Distinguish clearly between:
  - widely attested patterns
  - moderately attested patterns
  - single-language observations
- Avoid theoretical terminology; use descriptive language grounded in the examples.